            <title>[LU-21047] sanity test_243: group_lock_test test40 hangs in client write/writeback (timeout)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21047</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_243 (group_lock_test test40) hangs on the client until the suite times out, with a Lustre client write/writeback deadlock under a group lock.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test set: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/f2edae71-b702-46e9-9834-1daef2f777f1" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/f2edae71-b702-46e9-9834-1daef2f777f1&lt;/a&gt; (review-dne-zfs-part-1, el10.1 zfs, DNE, 4 MDT / 8 OST, kernel 6.12)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;group_lock_test test40 takes a GROUP lock (gid 1234) and forks 40 children, each doing pwritev() of 10000 bytes at offset 10000*i, so neighbouring writers share 4K pages. test10..test30 pass; test40 never finishes ("Starting test test40" is the last line of the suite log) and the session times out after 331 minutes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client stacks at the timeout:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The OSC brw_queue_work kworker is stuck in folio_wait_bit_common() &amp;lt;- cl_page_make_ready() (folio_lock) &amp;lt;- osc_extent_make_ready() &amp;lt;- osc_send_write_rpc().&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Several group_lock_test children are in D state in folio_wait_writeback() &amp;lt;- cl_page_assume() &amp;lt;- ll_write_begin() &amp;lt;- vvp_io_write_start().&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;osc_extent_wait() reports the extent &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;0 -&amp;gt; 255/255&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; in state "locking", flags wiY, under the GROUP lock, "wait ext to 0 timedout".&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;It looks like a lock-order cycle: the writeback worker holds earlier pages of an RPC in writeback and waits for the folio lock of a page that a writer holds while waiting for writeback of a page already in that RPC. The RPC cannot be sent, so writeback never ends.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not a duplicate of &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15951" title="sanity test_243: A group lock test failed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15951"&gt;LU-15951&lt;/a&gt; (assertion in test30, different failure). Similar symptom to &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19951" title="Deadlock between kswapd writeback and writer extent hold" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19951"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19951&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (fixed in 7dc7cffb11, which is in the tested tree), but the extent here is in "locking" state, not "active".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen once in 2451 review runs of this group over 30 days. Found on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/67604" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/67604&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19722" title="PFL: append of PFL file should not use 'append_stripe_count' layout" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19722"&gt;LU-19722&lt;/a&gt; llite: send NO_APPEND flag from client), whose changes do not touch the client I/O path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-67604-ps23-569c11ba5aa5 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/67604" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/67604&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
